  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established and satisfies all constraints. The minimum power_index achieved is 1.75 (pipelined_m, data_width=17, n_iter=15, m=3), which is significantly lower than the HV reference of 40. The accuracy_bits range from 12.7 to 14.4, comfortably exceeding the HV reference of 12 and the constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-12 (approx 12 bits). Throughput is consistently >= 50 MSPS for all front designs (51.9 to 132 MSPS). The front covers a meaningful trade-off curve between power and accuracy. Since this is the final round and the front is stable with good hypervolume coverage (88.72), stopping is the appropriate action."
